---
import Callout from "~/components/illustration-kit/Callout.astro"
import IllustrationFigure from "~/components/illustration-kit/IllustrationFigure.astro"

const tosses = ["T", "H", "H", "H"]
---

<IllustrationFigure lead="Why can THH beat HHH when both patterns are equally likely in three tosses?">
  <p class="text-base leading-normal">
    The first player picks <strong>HHH</strong>. The second picks <strong>THH</strong>. H means
    heads and T means tails. Follow the results from left to right.
  </p>

  <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-4 gap-2 text-center sm:gap-3">
      {tosses.map((toss, index) => (
        <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-1">
          <span class="text-sm">Toss {index + 1}</span>
          <span
            class:list={[
              "flex h-11 w-11 items-center justify-center rounded-full border-2 border-ink text-lg font-bold",
              index === 3 && "border-dashed",
            ]}
          >
            {toss}
          </span>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <p class="text-base leading-normal">
        <strong>THH appears in tosses 1–3, so it wins first.</strong>
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-4 gap-2 text-center sm:gap-3" aria-hidden="true">
        {tosses.slice(0, 3).map((toss) => (
          <span class="border-t-4 border-series-blue bg-series-blue/10 py-2 font-bold">
            {toss}
          </span>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <p class="text-base leading-normal">
        <strong>HHH would appear in tosses 2–4, but too late.</strong>
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-4 gap-2 text-center sm:gap-3" aria-hidden="true">
        <span></span>
        {tosses.slice(1).map((toss) => (
          <span class="border-t-4 border-series-red bg-series-red/10 py-2 font-bold">
            {toss}
          </span>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="text-base leading-normal">
    The dashed fourth toss is hypothetical: the game stops after toss 3, when THH wins.
    It is shown to reveal the overlap.
  </p>

  <Callout tone="accent">
    <p class="leading-normal">
      <strong>Why THH wins 7 times in 8:</strong> HHH can win only if the first three tosses are
      HHH, a 1 in 8 chance. Otherwise, the first eventual HHH must follow a tail, making THH
      appear one toss earlier.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <Fragment slot="caption">
    The patterns overlap. Each has a 1 in 8 chance in any fixed group of three tosses, but that
    does not give them equal chances of appearing first.
  </Fragment>
</IllustrationFigure>
